symbol write_retry
lines 0 19
hash fe830c975769481d
note Every file the tool writes, the map and the cache alike, goes through here: the bytes land in a temporary file beside the target and are renamed over it, so a reader, or the second of two threads saving at once, never sees a half-written file. A sharing violation from an editor or scanner holding the file is retried a few times.

